1
00:01:16,232 --> 00:01:19,145
Revenue Bird

2
00:01:25,308 --> 00:01:27,117
So boring!

3
00:01:38,421 --> 00:01:40,332
If you want to see it, go to buy it!

4
00:01:42,358 --> 00:01:45,703
I will buy it if I have enough money.

5
00:01:46,863 --> 00:01:49,036
Hi, Nobita!

6
00:01:49,099 --> 00:01:51,101
Why are you napping here?

7
00:01:51,167 --> 00:01:53,010
Thanks for coming!

8
00:01:53,736 --> 00:01:56,012
I've bought 10 new publishing books!

9
00:01:59,642 --> 00:02:01,747
Ah, you bought 10 books, Suneo?

10
00:02:01,811 --> 00:02:03,290
I won't lend it to you to read.

11
00:02:03,346 --> 00:02:04,950
I bought it with my pocket money.

12
00:02:05,014 --> 00:02:07,426
I think men must live equally.

13
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:10,329
Don't we have no ideas to
change this wrong world?

14
00:02:10,353 --> 00:02:11,889
It's really too unfair!

15
00:02:11,955 --> 00:02:14,367
Suneo always enjoys the privilege.

16
00:02:15,191 --> 00:02:18,866
Yet we still have some ways
that can make people live equally.

17
00:02:18,928 --> 00:02:21,204
Revenue Bird

18
00:02:22,232 --> 00:02:24,906
We can gather tax from the pocket money.

19
00:02:24,968 --> 00:02:27,744
For example,
your have 500 Yen pocket money.

20
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:30,444
It'll take 50 Yen from it.

21
00:02:30,473 --> 00:02:34,819
No jokes! I'm troublesome for
I haven't enough money to use.

22
00:02:34,844 --> 00:02:37,825
But more money, more tax!

23
00:02:37,881 --> 00:02:39,519
If the money is over 1 thousand,
the tax rate will be 3 percent.

24
00:02:39,582 --> 00:02:41,391
And if it's over 10 thousand,
the tax rate will be 7 percent.

25
00:02:41,417 --> 00:02:43,897
Thus will be a little bit fair.

26
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:47,493
And then use the collecting revenue
to buy something useful to us.

27
00:02:47,557 --> 00:02:49,366
It must be decided by we all.

28
00:02:49,392 --> 00:02:52,635
The problem is
whether everyone will agree.

29
00:02:53,329 --> 00:02:54,899
Go to discuss with everyone.

30
00:02:56,766 --> 00:03:00,111
We've never heard so good idea,
have we, everyone?

31
00:03:00,136 --> 00:03:03,948
Nobita, you're so smart.

32
00:03:03,973 --> 00:03:07,182
Use the revenue to make uniform
of Gian's team.

33
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:09,554
And
build an appropriative baseball ground.

34
00:03:09,579 --> 00:03:11,490
And form a baseball team,

35
00:03:11,514 --> 00:03:12,891
Furthermore, set up a building.
Inside there're some restaurants,

36
00:03:12,916 --> 00:03:17,194
electronic playrooms, resting rooms.
And we can pull the pin.

37
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:18,631
You did go too much!

38
00:03:18,655 --> 00:03:21,101
Actually you don't need to do that.

39
00:03:21,124 --> 00:03:23,229
Buy whatever you would like to buy,
everyone!

40
00:03:23,293 --> 00:03:25,773
I hope you can use them freely.

41
00:03:25,795 --> 00:03:28,332
Shut up! I agree, okay?

42
00:03:29,098 --> 00:03:31,669
Everyone is happy and agree to it.

43
00:03:32,769 --> 00:03:34,476
So let's do it!

44
00:03:35,638 --> 00:03:37,914
Now it's checking the pocket money
of everyone.

45
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:42,950
Doraemon, you have 100 Yen.

46
00:03:43,012 --> 00:03:44,719
So you shall pay 10 Yen.

47
00:03:44,747 --> 00:03:47,284
I did expect to buy Rice Cracker with it

48
00:03:48,718 --> 00:03:50,629
Here is you change, 90 Yen!

49
00:03:51,888 --> 00:03:54,630
It's well enough that
I have no money with me now.

50
00:03:55,191 --> 00:03:58,172
What're you saying?
Now we'll go to your homes

51
00:03:58,194 --> 00:04:00,902
and take the money from
your saving box as the revenue.

52
00:04:01,831 --> 00:04:03,401
That's the way to my home!

53
00:04:03,466 --> 00:04:05,468
Hey, wait! Don't go there!

54
00:04:11,574 --> 00:04:13,554
Oh, my saving box!

55
00:04:15,612 --> 00:04:21,688
There're 23,046 Yen in all!
The revenue is 16,132 Yen.

56
00:04:21,751 --> 00:04:24,527
Oh, no! That's all of mine!

57
00:04:26,222 --> 00:04:27,860
Thank you!

58
00:04:28,191 --> 00:04:30,671
It's collecting the revenue strictly.

59
00:04:30,693 --> 00:04:32,172
It seems can collect lots of money.

60
00:04:32,228 --> 00:04:35,141
I've spent my deposit money
and pocket money earlier,

61
00:04:35,164 --> 00:04:37,144
so I can take it easy!

62
00:04:37,166 --> 00:04:38,406
I'm back!

63
00:04:38,434 --> 00:04:40,675
Welcome back! Here is your
pocket money of this month, 500 Yen!

64
00:04:40,703 --> 00:04:43,513
But you don't need to
give it to me at this moment.

65
00:04:44,374 --> 00:04:45,284
Revenue

66
00:04:45,308 --> 00:04:47,185
I'll pay! I'll pay for it, okay?

67
00:04:47,210 --> 00:04:49,190
This is strict indeed!

68
00:04:51,247 --> 00:04:52,225
Hi!

69
00:04:52,248 --> 00:04:53,727
Uncle Nobi!

70
00:04:53,750 --> 00:04:56,594
I'll go to Indian again.
And I'll stay there about 3 years!

71
00:04:56,619 --> 00:04:59,600
So I'll give you gifts of money
of 3 years in advance.

72
00:05:00,523 --> 00:05:01,399
Here you are!

73
00:05:01,424 --> 00:05:02,528
30 thousand Yen!

74
00:05:02,592 --> 00:05:04,162
I won't take it...

75
00:05:04,227 --> 00:05:06,673
Oh? It's not you work-style!
Just take it!

76
00:05:07,530 --> 00:05:09,703
Bye, we can't see each other
for a while. Take care!

77
00:05:10,133 --> 00:05:11,373
Wait, Uncle!

78
00:05:11,401 --> 00:05:13,608
You don't need to give me money!
It's okay that you have such thought.

79
00:05:14,137 --> 00:05:16,117
Revenue 11,100 Yen!

80
00:05:18,808 --> 00:05:20,947
How is the revenue collecting going on?

81
00:05:21,010 --> 00:05:23,183
Nobita, 22,500 Yen

82
00:05:23,246 --> 00:05:26,056
Shizuka, 11,200 Yen

83
00:05:26,082 --> 00:05:28,562
Desuki, 49,000 Yen

84
00:05:28,584 --> 00:05:31,258
Liu, 90,148 Yen

85
00:05:31,321 --> 00:05:33,301
Goda Gian, None

86
00:05:33,323 --> 00:05:35,325
Honekawa Suneo, None

87
00:05:36,693 --> 00:05:40,163
Suneo and Gian have no money?
So that means...

88
00:05:40,229 --> 00:05:42,300
Let's have a research!
Let's have a research!

89
00:05:42,365 --> 00:05:44,743
First, send off the finder!

90
00:05:47,670 --> 00:05:49,616
Then watch on TV!

91
00:05:55,912 --> 00:05:58,518
So we don't need pocket money at all!

92
00:06:00,917 --> 00:06:02,863
Is that cartoon? Let me have a read!

93
00:06:02,885 --> 00:06:04,831
How is it going on where Suneo is?

94
00:06:04,854 --> 00:06:07,767
Mom, do you want me to buy something?

95
00:06:07,790 --> 00:06:10,134
No, nothing!

96
00:06:10,159 --> 00:06:13,106
Didn't I bring you
all the deposit money just now?

97
00:06:13,129 --> 00:06:14,904
Please take the money from it.

98
00:06:14,931 --> 00:06:18,970
I hope you ask me to buy the
exercise necessaries with it.

99
00:06:19,469 --> 00:06:21,506
I'll give it to mom
after I bought it home.

100
00:06:21,571 --> 00:06:23,448
And it'll be good
if mom give it back to me!

101
00:06:25,041 --> 00:06:26,748
Revenue Bird

102
00:06:26,776 --> 00:06:29,052
Go to find Suneo for the revenue!

103
00:06:29,946 --> 00:06:32,085
Except the pocket money,
you can't ask him for revenue!

104
00:06:32,148 --> 00:06:33,627
Oh, you can't!

105
00:06:33,649 --> 00:06:35,128
Oh, it's so heavy!

106
00:06:36,753 --> 00:06:39,290
That's what mom asked me to buy!

107
00:06:42,792 --> 00:06:44,772
Isn't the revenue too high?

108
00:06:44,827 --> 00:06:46,807
You're too much!

109
00:06:46,863 --> 00:06:50,276
I saved those money so hard for
I was eager to buy a microscope.

110
00:06:50,299 --> 00:06:53,678
And I even went to teach
the neighbor's children in spare time.

111
00:06:53,703 --> 00:06:55,182
Because saving money is my fun!

112
00:06:55,238 --> 00:06:57,878
I didn't even go it on something
I wanted to buy.

113
00:06:59,108 --> 00:07:01,588
We can't stop Revenue Bird!

114
00:07:02,078 --> 00:07:04,080
Hey, have you collected lots of revenues

115
00:07:05,415 --> 00:07:07,326
Can we buy something now?

116
00:07:07,350 --> 00:07:09,023
10 Yen, it's great!

117
00:07:09,085 --> 00:07:12,658
One percent of the revenue is 1 Yen!
Take it out quickly!

118
00:07:13,222 --> 00:07:16,135
Bastard!
Go and ask for it from the richer men!

119
00:07:29,038 --> 00:07:32,781
Great! The machine can't work, so the
game of collecting revenues is over!

120
00:07:32,809 --> 00:07:35,688
Too great...

121
00:07:42,718 --> 00:07:46,291
Weather Cushion!

122
00:07:46,823 --> 00:07:48,928
Now it's time to broadcast the news
about children!

123
00:07:48,991 --> 00:07:50,595
Today we'll go to see

124
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:53,334
what games will the children in Tokyo

125
00:07:53,396 --> 00:07:54,534
play in cold weather?

126
00:07:54,597 --> 00:07:56,008
Mr. Santen!

127
00:07:56,032 --> 00:07:57,534
Okay, I'm Mr. Santen!

128
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,578
Everyone, please look here!

129
00:07:58,634 --> 00:08:00,113
I believe everyone can see that

130
00:08:00,136 --> 00:08:02,309
our lively little friends
are kicking up a din!

131
00:08:02,371 --> 00:08:05,818
Let me interview these little friends!

132
00:08:05,875 --> 00:08:07,684
Don't you feel cold?

133
00:08:07,710 --> 00:08:08,916
No, we don't!

134
00:08:08,978 --> 00:08:10,787
You're in high spirits!

135
00:08:10,813 --> 00:08:12,417
Such extent of cold is
a piece of cake to us!

136
00:08:12,482 --> 00:08:13,790
Wow, you're great!

137
00:08:13,816 --> 00:08:14,817
$0 you?

138
00:08:14,884 --> 00:08:16,227
You don't feel cold?

139
00:08:16,252 --> 00:08:17,754
Circumfused by
the spirited little friends,

140
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:19,663
I feel my body gets warmer and warmer.

141
00:08:19,689 --> 00:08:21,999
Here above is play-by-play story
of the locale.

142
00:08:22,024 --> 00:08:24,300
Well, I'll invite Nobita to
go outside to play.

143
00:08:25,328 --> 00:08:27,137
Nobita

144
00:08:27,530 --> 00:08:29,567
What's the matter, Doraemon?

145
00:08:30,199 --> 00:08:33,646
Don't keep staying at home!
You'd go outside to play sometimes.

146
00:08:33,703 --> 00:08:35,205
Though I'd like to say that to you,

147
00:08:35,271 --> 00:08:37,308
you won't go, right?
Because it's cold outside.

148
00:08:37,373 --> 00:08:39,046
You know my thoughts so well.

149
00:08:39,108 --> 00:08:42,146
Anyway, it's no funny to go outside.

150
00:08:42,211 --> 00:08:44,213
It'll be bad if we have a cold.

151
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:45,884
But it'll be something else again
if it snows.

152
00:08:45,948 --> 00:08:48,360
If it snows,
you'll go outside to play, will you?

153
00:08:48,384 --> 00:08:50,295
Well, if so...

154
00:08:52,054 --> 00:08:54,295
Machine can awake snow

155
00:08:55,258 --> 00:08:57,238
Weather Cushion!

156
00:08:57,260 --> 00:08:59,672
This is the textbook for the students
in the future world.

157
00:08:59,695 --> 00:09:04,075
It can experience snow or wind
and all kinds of other stuffs.

158
00:09:04,467 --> 00:09:07,414
For example,
if you press button Windy No. 1!

159
00:09:08,037 --> 00:09:11,484
There will be high and low
air pressure places on the cushion

160
00:09:11,541 --> 00:09:13,748
It'll cause the air flowing!

161
00:09:13,776 --> 00:09:15,255
Really!

162
00:09:15,278 --> 00:09:17,884
And if you
press the button of clouds next,

163
00:09:17,947 --> 00:09:18,925
I know,

164
00:09:18,948 --> 00:09:21,485
the vapor in the air will cool down
and change to small waterdrop.

165
00:09:21,551 --> 00:09:23,792
And they'll gather to be clouds.

166
00:09:24,086 --> 00:09:26,430
While you press the button of raining,

167
00:09:26,856 --> 00:09:30,133
the waterdrops inside the bank of clouds
will get bigger and heavier and drop!

168
00:09:30,159 --> 00:09:33,003
What're you doing?
The water drops to the ground.

169
00:09:33,362 --> 00:09:34,363
Oh, bad!

170
00:09:34,430 --> 00:09:36,068
Let's go outside to
do the experiment a while later.

171
00:09:36,132 --> 00:09:38,112
Perhaps it'll thunder too!

172
00:09:40,703 --> 00:09:42,876
Line up the cushions!

173
00:09:42,939 --> 00:09:44,816
And broaden the area!

174
00:09:46,842 --> 00:09:48,617
What kinds of snow do you like?

175
00:09:48,644 --> 00:09:51,147
Of course white and thick snow it is!

176
00:09:51,614 --> 00:09:55,027
If you want to ski,
then it's better to be thin.

177
00:09:55,051 --> 00:09:57,759
And if you want to pile snowman,
then stretches of snow will be better.

178
00:09:57,787 --> 00:09:58,822
So,

179
00:09:58,888 --> 00:10:00,265
stretches of snow!

180
00:10:00,289 --> 00:10:01,927
I know!

181
00:10:05,461 --> 00:10:08,340
Rain will change to snow while
in lower temperature!

182
00:10:08,364 --> 00:10:09,900
Yeah!

183
00:10:10,433 --> 00:10:12,435
It seems hard to snow.

184
00:10:12,501 --> 00:10:16,074
Doraemon, when can we pile snowman

185
00:10:16,138 --> 00:10:18,482
About 20 or 30 minutes later!

186
00:10:18,507 --> 00:10:20,487
Well, then call me when it snows!

187
00:10:26,482 --> 00:10:28,758
Hey, it's already snowed!

188
00:10:28,784 --> 00:10:30,229
Okay!

189
00:10:31,487 --> 00:10:33,933
I'll pile a big snowman!

190
00:10:33,956 --> 00:10:35,230
Do your best!

191
00:10:35,257 --> 00:10:37,498
Hah, so it is!

192
00:10:41,130 --> 00:10:42,302
Oh, so cold!

193
00:10:42,365 --> 00:10:43,673
Doraemon

194
00:10:43,699 --> 00:10:45,701
I have a strange question to ask.

195
00:10:45,768 --> 00:10:47,839
Though you have good abilities,

196
00:10:47,903 --> 00:10:50,509
you can't turn the snow warm, right?

197
00:10:50,573 --> 00:10:53,782
I'll help you whatever trouble you have!

198
00:10:54,543 --> 00:10:56,921
It should be laid nearby!

199
00:10:56,946 --> 00:10:58,084
Found it!

200
00:10:58,147 --> 00:11:01,128
There're all kinds of disks! Use this!

201
00:11:02,451 --> 00:11:04,522
Oh, so warm!

202
00:11:07,023 --> 00:11:08,832
The temperature
makes me feel comfortable!

203
00:11:08,858 --> 00:11:10,394
So heavy!

204
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:15,006
Couldn't I pile a snowman
without others help?

205
00:11:17,299 --> 00:11:20,303
Don't go too far! What am I here for...

206
00:11:21,504 --> 00:11:24,110
Leave you alone! Do it by yourself?

207
00:11:25,775 --> 00:11:28,449
A robot would go on the bend too!
It's shameful!

208
00:11:30,413 --> 00:11:32,290
He lost the disks here!

209
00:11:32,314 --> 00:11:34,624
What! How could it be?

210
00:11:39,789 --> 00:11:42,360
What! Just a part of it!

211
00:12:01,677 --> 00:12:03,850
Thus is relaxed! Really good!

212
00:12:04,146 --> 00:12:06,626
There're many kinds of disks!

213
00:12:07,016 --> 00:12:08,757
White snow! Its pronunciation
in Japanese sounds like castle's!

214
00:12:08,784 --> 00:12:10,923
Originally, snow is white!

215
00:12:10,986 --> 00:12:13,057
Just make it snowing to have a look!

216
00:12:20,629 --> 00:12:22,540
Strange!

217
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:34,453
So-called white snow
is the castle in fact!

218
00:12:39,715 --> 00:12:41,888
Snow-ball-snow!

219
00:12:42,518 --> 00:12:44,088
Aren't they the snow-balls
used to play snow-battle?

220
00:12:44,153 --> 00:12:45,962
Let's invite Nobita to go together!

221
00:12:45,988 --> 00:12:50,698
But the brat must be in his warm home!

222
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:54,068
Gian, you look! Does Nobita
have such stuffs in his home?

223
00:12:54,096 --> 00:12:55,074
What stuffs?

224
00:12:55,097 --> 00:12:56,735
Strange! Isn't that a castle?

225
00:12:56,799 --> 00:12:59,405
Yeah, and it's made of snow!

226
00:13:02,505 --> 00:13:04,951
Nobita, where is the castle from?

227
00:13:04,974 --> 00:13:06,920
I made it!

228
00:13:06,942 --> 00:13:08,922
Yeah, let's play a snow-battle!

229
00:13:08,978 --> 00:13:10,355
What

230
00:13:10,379 --> 00:13:12,325
Okay, let's play!

231
00:13:12,348 --> 00:13:14,521
Well, I made lots of snow-balls.

232
00:13:14,583 --> 00:13:17,063
We can almost begin!

233
00:13:17,086 --> 00:13:18,087
OK

234
00:13:18,154 --> 00:13:19,792
Well, let's begin!

235
00:13:23,893 --> 00:13:26,169
I won't be hit by Nobita's snow-ball!

236
00:13:26,195 --> 00:13:27,731
I won't...

237
00:13:28,464 --> 00:13:31,274
Run away quickly...

238
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:34,110
Great! I won Gian!

239
00:13:34,136 --> 00:13:36,480
Nobita, you're great!

240
00:13:37,606 --> 00:13:39,017
This is the last sheet of clouds!

241
00:13:39,041 --> 00:13:40,679
Women Snow!

242
00:13:41,710 --> 00:13:44,190
This seems interesting!

243
00:13:47,483 --> 00:13:48,894
Why hasn't he come in yet?

244
00:13:48,918 --> 00:13:50,056
Isn't it matter?

245
00:13:50,119 --> 00:13:53,100
Nobita is so enjoying himself outside
that he'd not like to come in! It's rare

246
00:13:55,524 --> 00:13:57,902
Help... Doraemon

247
00:13:57,927 --> 00:14:00,168
Snow-girl is chasing me!

248
00:14:00,196 --> 00:14:03,336
Let's play the game together!

249
00:14:09,905 --> 00:14:13,682
Change to clouds?

250
00:14:19,181 --> 00:14:22,424
Doraemon, you'd help me
with my homework on occasion.

251
00:14:22,451 --> 00:14:24,624
I can't do that!

252
00:14:27,356 --> 00:14:30,303
Clouds in the guy can fly leisurely,
that's great!

253
00:14:30,326 --> 00:14:32,704
Geez! I can't stand...

254
00:14:32,728 --> 00:14:34,036
Oh, you are noisy!

255
00:14:34,063 --> 00:14:36,509
What! Do you still think
it's no matter with you?

256
00:14:36,532 --> 00:14:37,943
Can't help!

257
00:14:37,967 --> 00:14:41,346
You seem get along with your homework
slowly! Would you like to have a rest?

258
00:14:41,370 --> 00:14:43,680
To have a rest... What to do?

259
00:14:43,706 --> 00:14:45,879
Didn't you want to be clouds?

260
00:14:45,941 --> 00:14:48,114
